# The tools this repo's checks run on, one `<tool> <version>` per line. lint/check_tool_pins.py compares them to the machine.
# The python line is read by actions/setup-python, so a comment never sits after it.
# read: python = python3 --version
# read: python = python --version
python 3.15
git 2.56
# A fix line gives the command that brings a tool up to its pin on one platform; the owner runs it. No Linux line until the owner names a Linux machine.
# fix: python macos = brew upgrade python@3.15
# fix: python windows = winget upgrade --id Python.Python.3.15 -e
# fix: git macos = brew upgrade git
# fix: git windows = winget upgrade --id Git.Git -e
